values ((select id from verses where ref='1.1.1' and work_id=(select id from works where slug='bhagavata-purana')), (select id from editions where slug='sb-wm-en'),
        'janma-ādi — birth and the rest (sustenance, dissolution)
asya — of this (universe)
yataḥ — from whom
anvayāt itarataḥ ca — by presence (in all things) and by distinctness (from them)
artheṣu abhijñaḥ — fully aware of all objects
svarāṭ — self-luminous, independent
tene — imparted
brahma — the Veda
hṛdā — through the heart
yaḥ — who
ādi-kavaye — to the first seer (Brahmā)
muhyanti — are bewildered
yat — about whom
sūrayaḥ — the wise
tejaḥ-vāri-mṛdām — of fire, water and earth
yathā — just as
vinimayaḥ — mutual confusion / exchange
yatra — in whom
tri-sargaḥ — the threefold creation (of the guṇas)
amṛṣā — (appears) not false, real
dhāmnā svena — by his own radiance
sadā — always
nirasta-kuhakam — who has dispelled deception (māyā)
satyam param — the supreme truth
